 ## Background
-The Octree Volume Structure was introduced in the context of interactive isosurface ray tracing of large volumes. It was developed to address the memory and performance limitations of uncompressed structured data and standard octree representations [S1, S2]. The method builds upon earlier work on octrees for faster isosurface generation [S28] and real-time exploration of regular volume data [S26]. The specific optimization of using parent-based storage with cap nodes and embedded scalar leaves was detailed in the paper "Interactive Isosurface Ray Tracing of Large Octree Volumes" [S1, S2].
